  "root_cause_and_fix": {
    "symptom": "FLIP 5->6 with three residents: new kernel found no handoff pair, booted clean (No committed state found), residents lost; recorder on the next boot: HOPOS_FLIP_STALLED step 12/11. FLIP 1->5 on an empty node left the node dark (watchdog silenced before the boot guard armed).",
    "cause": "uncommitted kernflip change (18 September, O6N work) relocated the handoff pointer/magic pair to the borrowed window offset because the UEFI boot scratch lies inside the kernel window; Apple, Pi, RK3566, QEMU and LicheeRV use a fixed cpuinit scratch, so the incoming kernel read the fixed address and found nothing. Only departures from older kernels (installed kernel, 9 September kernel) still worked.",
    "fix": "kernflip.BoardScratchInWindow, set only by board_uefi.go and board_o6n.go; the pair is relocated only there. metal/kern/kernflip/flip.go, metal/cmd/hopos/board_uefi.go, metal/cmd/hopos/board_o6n.go.",
    "verification": "QEMU flip regression (image/qemu-run.sh flip): HOPOS_FLIP_OK, two residents survived 3 kernel flips, NAT and pool checks OK (qemu-flip-regression-after-fix.log). The later demo step \"FAIL smc-kooi: slot 2 still owns memory\" is unrelated to the flip and not investigated. M4: flips 11->12->13 adopt 3/3 residents with held TCP sockets.",
    "poisoned_state_note": "two clean boots over live parked cores left the M4 unable to start a second app core (apple: cpu2 did not start, HOPOS_PART_QUARANTINE); a power cycle restored it. Not counted as evidence."
  },
